{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-320b-7079-a323-c4b331072571","id":"01a1a667-4d6a-7186-9195-f76f90d55346","idempotency_key":"6d7db8a6d8151ea13d21c2d510c0295c5671a28210ff96b1f6e7817011052054","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:52:30Z","payload":{"note":"Closed 5/5. ./scripts/check_studies.sh is the one command: storage (CRUD, order, revisions, versions, progress), the tools and their locks, the approval gate, the bundle round trip, and the browser editor, ending in STUDY_SUITE_PASS - 89 tests. It reuses a healthy server on 8090 or starts one on a scratch database, so it runs from a cold checkout instead of only on a machine where someone left the app running; check_all.sh calls it. The one REAL gap it filled was i-4d4e: approvals had been tested for board writes only, so crates/ai/tests/study_authoring_approval.rs now asserts that a study write needs approval, that a BOARD-WRITE grant does NOT let study content through (different scopes, different promises), that only StudyContent changes the answer, that an in-app grant does not leak to MCP, and that an approved create_study then applies and its study takes a chapter. Everything else on this checklist already existed from the tickets that built it: db.rs/foundation.rs for CRUD and order, study_bundle.rs for the round trip with unknown fields, study_progress.rs for isolation and content neutrality.","target":"t-5ede"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
